---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import { APP_URL, salesMailto } from '../../site';
---

<Base
  title="Docs · CAN Data Extract"
  description="Getting started with the CAN Data Extract online app and desktop app, and how CAN Data Extract writes frames, services and units."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <Eyebrow>Docs</Eyebrow>
      <h1 class="display-2 page-head__title">Getting started.</h1>
      <p class="lede page-head__lede">
        The short version for both apps. Full reference documentation is being written; until it
        is published, write to <a href={salesMailto('CAN Data Extract docs question')}>sales</a> with questions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container docs">
    <nav class="docs__toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="label">On this page</p>
      <a href="#online">Online app</a>
      <a href="#desktop">Desktop app</a>
      <a href="#notation">Reading frames</a>
      <a href="#support">Formats and adapters</a>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <h2 id="online">Online app</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Sign in.</strong> Open <a href={APP_URL}>app.candataextract.com</a> and sign in with Google, Microsoft Entra ID, a password or a passkey.</li>
        <li><strong>Open a namespace.</strong> Access is by invite. Your private namespace, or a team namespace you were invited to, appears in the namespace selector after you open it once.</li>
        <li><strong>Import a trace.</strong> Add a candump log, PCAN TRC, VCDS, ODIS or MF4 file to a collection. The frame table loads it with ISO-TP streams reassembled.</li>
        <li><strong>Decode.</strong> Select a row to open the byte decoder. Hover a field to see its bytes.</li>
        <li><strong>Add a transform.</strong> Write a CEL expression that picks a value out of a payload, check the highlighted matches, and save it to the namespace.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="desktop">Desktop app</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Connect an adapter.</strong> SocketCAN on Linux (<code>can0</code>), PCAN on macOS and Windows (<code>PCAN_USBBUS1</code>). Set the bus bitrate, usually <code>500 kbit/s</code> for diagnostics on passenger cars.</li>
        <li><strong>Record.</strong> Start a capture, run your diagnostic tool or the built-in scan, and stop. Save the capture locally or stream it to a namespace.</li>
        <li><strong>Scan.</strong> Read the VIN, discover the manufacturer's ECUs, and read their data identifiers and fault codes.</li>
        <li><strong>Simulate.</strong> Build a simulator config from a capture and run it on a CAN interface, so a diagnostic tool can talk to the car without the car.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="notation">Reading frames</h2>
      <p>CAN Data Extract writes data the way the tools you already use do.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hex</strong> is uppercase, two digits per byte, one space between bytes: <code>02 10 03</code>. The <code>0x</code> prefix appears only for a single value in prose, as in "service 0x10".</li>
        <li><strong>Frames</strong> are written <code>ID#DATA</code>, the cansend form. IDs are three digits for 11-bit (<code>7E0</code>) and eight for 29-bit (<code>18DA10F1</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Direction</strong> is a glyph: → request, ← response. A request is written before its response.</li>
        <li><strong>Services</strong> use the standard's names with their hex value: DiagnosticSessionControl (0x10), ReadDataByIdentifier (0x22).</li>
        <li><strong>Negative responses</strong> name the NRC on first mention: NRC 0x78 (requestCorrectlyReceived-ResponsePending), <code>7F 10 78</code> inside a payload.</li>
        <li><strong>Time</strong> is ISO 8601 with a zone, <code>2024-10-22T09:40:26.489Z</code>. Deltas in tables have six decimals: <code>+0.000124 s</code>.</li>
      </ul>
<pre><code>→ 7E0#02 10 03                DiagnosticSessionControl (0x10), extended session
← 7E8#06 50 03 00 32 01 F4    positive response, P2 = 50 ms, P2* = 5000 ms</code></pre>

      <h2 id="support">Formats and adapters</h2>
      <dl class="docs__dl">
        <dt>Protocols</dt><dd>UDS (ISO 14229), KWP2000, OBD, ISO-TP, CAN FD, 11-bit and 29-bit IDs</dd>
        <dt>Trace formats</dt><dd>candump log, PCAN TRC, VCDS, ODIS, MF4</dd>
        <dt>Adapters</dt><dd>SocketCAN on Linux, PCAN on macOS and Windows</dd>
        <dt>Sign-in</dt><dd>Google, Microsoft Entra ID, password, passkey</dd>
      </dl>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head { padding-block: var(--space-24) 0; }
  .page-head__title { margin-top: var(--space-6); color: var(--ink); }
  .page-head__lede { margin-top: var(--space-10); }

  .docs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-16); padding-top: var(--space-8); }
  .docs > * { min-width: 0; }
  .docs__toc { position: sticky; top: var(--space-10); align-self: start; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-4); margin-top: var(--space-16); font-size: 14px; }
  .docs__toc .label { text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .docs__toc a { color: var(--ink-muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .docs__toc a:hover { color: var(--trace); }
  .docs__dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 140px 1fr; gap: var(--space-5) var(--space-8); }
  .docs__dl dt { font: 500 10px/22px var(--font-sans); letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .docs__dl dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .docs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
    .docs__toc { position: static; }
    .docs__dl { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-2); }
    .docs__dl dd { margin-bottom: var(--space-5); }
  }
</style>
